# Development Standards

## Language

All code, comments, commit messages, PR descriptions, and skill outputs must be written in English.

## Test-first development (TDD)

TDD is mandatory for every feature and every fix, with no size-based exception. Always write the failing test before writing implementation code.

## No dead code

Never leave dead code, unused variables, or unused imports in code that is committed.

## Conventional Commits

Every commit must follow Conventional Commits format, and must always include both:

- a concise, explicit subject line
- a body explaining what changed and why
